  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Electrical Contractors and Other Wiring Installation Contractors (NAICS 238210) has $552M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The market recorded 2,298 awards so far, with an average award size of $240K. Obligations fell 30.2% year over year. Obligations peaked at $945M in FY23 and then moved to $824M in FY24 and $791M in FY25 before reaching $552M in FY26. The Department of Defense, the Department of Veterans Affairs, and the Department of State are the top buyers this fiscal year, obligating $138M, $118M, and $111M respectively. XATOR LLC, SINTELA INC, and WSP USA SOLUTIONS INC are the largest vendors by obligations in FY2026 to date, with $78.5M, $36.3M, and $33.2M respectively. This profile highlights a market that remains sizable but smaller than the recent peak years, concentrated among a handful of federal buyers and prime contractors.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 30.2% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations moved from $945M in FY23, to $824M in FY24, to $791M in FY25, and to $552M in FY26. The FY26 total of $552M is below each of the three prior fiscal years listed."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors drive the FY2026 market?",
